From 4b49b5867fdd033a24cea0391be8e20fd2351547 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lovelace's Square <noreply@lovelacesquare.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:41:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Let assistants connect: a setting that opens every
 window's control channel

A window opened from the file manager has no control port, so an
assistant the user works with (an MCP client, say) cannot join the
window the user is working in. File > Options gets an Agents section with
"Let assistants connect to this window", off by default. When on, a
window started without --control opens its control channel as
`--control auto` does (a free port, the key file named after it); the
key is still required on every request.

- ui-egui: UiState::allow_assistants (allowAssistants in ui.json; off
  when missing or not `true`, without failing the other settings), the
  `ui.allowAssistants` command (`on`, alias `value`; without it the
  setting is read, never toggled, since it decides who may drive the
  app), listed in engine.commands, and the checkbox with a note in the
  Backstage options (not on the web, which has no control channel).
- gridcraft: the setting picks `auto` at start-up when no port was given;
  changed while running, it is saved at once (so windows opened next
  follow it) and turning it on opens this window's channel. Turning it
  off leaves an open channel until the window closes.
- docs: control-protocol.md.

